@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "How Recomp Works";
    ViewData["OnboardingPage"] = true;
}

<div class="onboarding-v11 onboarding-v12">

    <section class="ob11-hero">
        <div>
            <div class="marketing-kicker">WELCOME TO 12 WEEK RECOMP</div>
            <h1>Use your body to recompose it.</h1>
            <p>
                Your coaches and the individualized Recomp planning engine walk you through
                each day's exercise and nutrition plan so you can put the science into practice.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ob11-visual-lesson">
        <div class="ob11-visual-copy">
            <div class="marketing-kicker">YOUR FIRST LESSON</div>
            <h2>Toning is body recomposition.</h2>
            <p>
                More visible muscle and less body fat changes the look.
                The process is simple: work the muscle, refill the glycogen,
                and keep the overall weekly calorie deficit.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="ob11-poster">
            <img src="~/images/marketing-v11/recomp-four-stages.png"
                 alt="Four stages of women progressing from starting out to lean and toned" />
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ob11-three">
        <div class="marketing-kicker">THE 3 THINGS RECOMP KEEPS COORDINATED</div>
        <h2>Work. Refuel. Lean out.</h2>

        <div class="ob11-three-grid">
            <article>
                <span>1</span>
                <h3>Work the muscle</h3>
                <p>Resistance training uses glycogen and gives your body a reason to keep or build lean muscle.</p>
            </article>

            <article>
                <span>2</span>
                <h3>Refill glycogen</h3>
                <p>Carbohydrate restores training fuel. Protein stays high to support repair and lean tissue.</p>
            </article>

            <article>
                <span>3</span>
                <h3>Keep the weekly deficit</h3>
                <p>Your weekly calorie balance is what allows stored body fat to come down over time.</p>
            </article>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ob11-coaches">
        <div class="ob11-coach-copy">
            <div class="marketing-kicker">YOUR DAILY GUIDES</div>
            <h2>Cassie, Marisol, and the individualized Recomp planning engine.</h2>
            <p>
                Cassie is your main day-to-day coach for fueling and plan guidance.
                Marisol supports the training side. The planning engine keeps recalculating
                around the workouts you planned, the workouts you actually did, your intake,
                your recovery, and your progress.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="ob12-coach-portraits">
            <article>
                <img src="~/images/marketing-v12/coach-cassie-gym.png"
                     alt="Coach Cassie in a bright gym" />
                <strong>Cassie</strong>
                <span>Daily fueling and plan guidance</span>
            </article>

            <article>
                <img src="~/images/marketing-v12/coach-marisol-gym.png"
                     alt="Coach Marisol in a bright gym" />
                <strong>Marisol</strong>
                <span>Exercise and training guidance</span>
            </article>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ob11-process">
        <div class="marketing-kicker">WHAT YOU DO EACH DAY</div>
        <h2>Give Recomp a few real-world inputs. It keeps adjusting the plan.</h2>

        <div class="ob11-process-grid">
            <article>
                <b>1</b>
                <h3>Plan the workout</h3>
                <p>Tell Recomp what you intend to do.</p>
            </article>

            <article>
                <b>2</b>
                <h3>Log what happened</h3>
                <p>Planned and actual stay separate so the fuel math can change when the workout changes.</p>
            </article>

            <article>
                <b>3</b>
                <h3>Enter nutrition</h3>
                <p>Calories, protein, carbohydrate and fat tell Recomp what fuel actually came in.</p>
            </article>

            <article>
                <b>4</b>
                <h3>Check progress</h3>
                <p>Weight, body-composition context and trends help the plan improve over time.</p>
            </article>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ob11-engine">
        <div>
            <div class="marketing-kicker">THEN THE ENGINE ADAPTS</div>
            <h2>Your targets move with what actually happened.</h2>
        </div>

        <ul>
            <li>Estimates workout glycogen demand and recovery needs.</li>
            <li>Sets daily calorie, protein, carbohydrate and fat targets.</li>
            <li>Adjusts for prior intake and the next planned workload.</li>
            <li>Can recommend pre-workout carbohydrate when fuel looks short.</li>
            <li>Uses progress trends instead of treating one scale reading as the whole story.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="ob11-science">
        <div class="marketing-kicker">A FEW THINGS TO REMEMBER</div>

        <div class="ob11-note-grid">
            <article>
                <h3>Glycogen carries water</h3>
                <p>
                    Refilling muscle glycogen can temporarily move scale weight up.
                    That does not automatically mean body fat increased.
                </p>
            </article>

            <article>
                <h3>Protein stays high</h3>
                <p>
                    Protein supports muscle repair and preservation while the overall program
                    creates a controlled calorie deficit.
                </p>
            </article>

            <article>
                <h3>There is no magic food window</h3>
                <p>
                    Timing helps training and recovery, but calories and macros still matter.
                    Dessert can fit when it fits the day's plan.
                </p>
            </article>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ob11-start">
        <div>
            <div class="marketing-kicker">READY?</div>
            <h2>Give Recomp your baseline and planned week.</h2>
            <p>
                You do not need perfect data. Start with what you know.
                The system gets more useful as your actual data accumulates.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="ob11-start-actions">
            <a class="marketing-cta" asp-controller="Intake" asp-action="Index">Start My Setup</a>
            <a class="marketing-text-link" asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Evidence">Read the science</a>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="onboarding-sources">
        <strong>Science behind this explanation:</strong>
        <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26697098/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">glycogen availability and training adaptation</a>
        <span> | </span>
        <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/1901662/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">post-exercise glycogen restoration</a>
        <span> | </span>
        <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26817506/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">high-protein recomposition trial</a>
    </section>

</div>

<link rel="stylesheet"
      href="~/css/onboarding-v11.css"
      asp-append-version="true" />

